It is early evening, but the sun is still high in the sky.
We are sitting in the park on the grass.
Jonas and Nele are with me.
Jonas is standing at the grill.
"Are you hungry?" he asks.
"Yes, very!" Nele answers.
I take the bread rolls out of the backpack.
We eat together and talk.
"Did you barbecue often in Mexico?" Nele asks.
"Oh yes," I answer.
"Last year my family had a huge barbecue," I explain.
"The party was really big and almost everyone was there."
"Did you also have these little sausages there?" Jonas asks and laughs.
"No, we had different meat," I say.
"And the food was much spicier!"
We lie on the grass and relax.
It is almost nine o'clock, but it is still light.
"In Mexico, it was already dark at this time," I say.
"That is exactly the summer in Berlin," Jonas says.
I smile and enjoy the warm evening.
